First, try a tougher character.  A good one to start with is the Barbarian.

I usually play like this... First, stay in the regular levels until about
the 5th or 6th level.  You are almost certain to find some shops.  Get all
of the good stuff that you can, or steal if you're able.  On the way,
pick up the best armor and drop your old stuff.  You can get a 0 armor
class by finding one Dwarf with lots of stuff on him.  Hobbits also sometimes
where Elvin Mithril Mail, and Dwarvish Mithril is good too until you can
find better armor.

Your concerns before getting into the Mines: Good armor - around 0 AC, a
good weapon - Barbarians start out pretty good.  You'll get either a
battle axe or a two-handed sword.

Also, be especially watchful for altars.  Sacrifice everything you can
get your hands on, except undead creatures and your pet (and humans if
you're not chaotic.  That INCLUDES were-things.)  Doing this can get you
a nice weapon and lots of luck - which you will definitely need if you
ever want to get out alive.

I wouldn't go into the Mines until you have about 50 hitpoints and good
armor/weaponry.

